we begin with this for the second time  in less than a week a small jet has  crashed at an airport in flames and  miraculously everybody on board survived  again the twin-engine Cessna jet ran off  the runway yesterday at Auroville  Municipal Airport that's north of  Sacramento  authorities say the plane had problems  during takeoff the NTSB and FAA are  investigating Kris Van Cleave shows us  how remarkably everyone on the plane  survived flames poured from the  twin-engine Cessna Citation moments  after the jet skidded off in Northern  California runway Wednesday the plane  was headed from Orville to Portland  Oregon we don't know why but the pilots  aborted takeoff Zeke Higgins witnessed  what happened next I ended up going  inside in the pro shop telling the guys  about it I walked back out and on sudden  I see an explosion over there and the  planes gone eight passengers and two  pilots were on board everybody escaped  without injury the plane had 400 gallons  of jet fuel on board the burning  aircraft sparked a grass fire if you'd  have seen you know the enormous ball of  fire and smoke it's they're very very  lucky people the Cessna was a charter  operated by Delta private jets in a  statement the company said in part while  the cause of the incident is currently  under investigation we are providing  support to customers involved through  RIA Commendation and other resources  this is the second crash involving a  Cessna Citation jet in less than a week  okay everybody all right NASCAR legend  Dale Earnhardt jr. his wife and daughter  were landing in Tennessee last Thursday  when their plane crashed and caught fire  Earnhardt and family managed to escape  that crash alive  the Earnhardt crash involved a newer  model of the Cessna Citation than the  one that went off the runway yesterday  the accidents are different but as the  NTSB investigates they're certainly  going to be looking for any  commonalities that may have contributed  to the two fires we expect an update on  the Earnhardt crash in the coming days  Dale Earnhardt jr. says he'll be  attending an auto race this weekend  Tony glad everyone is okay Chris thank  you very much
 

